<title>MEXICO: ICA says GCarso leaves rail group.</title>
<headline>ICA says GCarso leaves rail group.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction company Empresas ICA said Tuesday that holding company Grupo Carso had pulled out of a syndicate to bid for forthcoming Mexican rail privatizations.</p>
<p>&quot;They (GCarso) are no longer with us, but was before,&quot; an ICA executive told Reuters.</p>
<p>GCarso had been part of a syndicate with ICA, Union Pacific Corp and Southwestern Bell Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;They (GCarso) did so because they wanted to. They were criticized as they have many interests in other businesses,&quot; he added, asking to remain anonymous.</p>
<p>ICA now has a 50-percent stake in the syndicate, while Union Pacific and Southern Bell have 25 percent each, he said.</p>
<p>-- Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617</p>
